labels: line 2 | line 3 | line 4 | line 5
answer: bcdef | fedcb | fedb | fd
wrong[bcdef | fedcba | feda | fd]: Each line works on the newest value of `s`. After line 2, s is "bcdef" (the a is gone), so reversing it gives "fedcb".
wrong[bcdef | fedcb | fedcb | fdb]: `s[:3]` stops before index 3, so it's only "fed". Adding the last character, b, gives "fedb".
